Hi Neetu,

I don’t fully understand. I just re-downloaded the file through the link I mentioned before, and obtained a ZIP of 532MB. This ZIP contains 24 HuGene 2.0 CEL files. Moreover, 24 HuGene 2.1 CEL files are included as well.

Indeed, I also concluded that yet no ST2.0 arrays are available through GEO. You have to realize that these 2.0 arrays are only on the market for less than a year or so, and it takes some time for labs to start using these chips, let alone to publish data that was generated. And it is only at that moment that submitting data to GEO or ArrayExpress is required.

Regards,

Guido

